	(gr_text "Route VSYS and VBAT as wide traces (≥0.5 mm, 0.8 mm is better), mostly on F.Cu. This is the simplest option.\nOr add a VSYS region on In2,\n\nSignals on F.Cu return through the solid GND on In1. Keep these on top and over unbroken ground:\n\nUSB D+/D−\nPDM_CLK and the I²S lines\nSPI_CLK\n\nUse B.Cu for slow lines: pull-ups, PWR_HOLD, CHG_STAT."
		(at 119.8 -8.3 0)
